WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.450
In the icy Southern Ocean,
trawlers haul in Antarctic krill.

2
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.610
The catch travels far.

3
00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:09.290
It ends up as krill oil
supplements on a shop shelf,

4
00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:11.790
and as feed for fish farms.

5
00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:16.150
And global demand for krill is an
economic pressure on the Southern Ocean.

6
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:20.170
So if the krill are
overfished, who actually loses?

7
00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.790
Only the fishing fleets?

8
00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.810
In this mission, you'll map
Antarctica and its climate,

9
00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:28.550
and find the line where its
ocean ecosystem really ends.

10
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:32.610
Then you'll weigh four
threats: climate change,

11
00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:35.270
fishing and whaling,
the search for minerals,

12
00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:37.370
and tourism and research.

13
00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:42.680
Your mission: decide who really loses if
the Southern Ocean's krill is overfished.
